---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Applicability"
   summary="Not every criterion applies to every page. a11ied makes that explicit so the report can say why a row matters, why it does not, or why the runtime still needs help from the operator."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Inputs that matter</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>document structure and semantics from the loaded target</li>
         <li>target hints from Storybook metadata or explicit CLI flags</li>
         <li>criterion-level rules baked into the WCAG engine</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Typical flow</h2>
      <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect applicable --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/auth-login.html --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect criterion 3.3.8 --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/auth-login.html --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         The first command asks what matters here. The second asks why one specific criterion is in or
         out. That sounds small, but it keeps later verification output from looking like a random dump
         of rows.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>What the output is doing</h2>
      <div class="mini-grid">
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Applicable</div>
            <p>The target contains cues that make the criterion relevant, like forms, dialogs, headings, landmarks, or live updates.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Not applicable</div>
            <p>The page simply does not have the structure or behavior that would trigger the criterion.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Needs review</div>
            <p>The target has weak signals and the runtime wants a human to settle the call instead of guessing.</p>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Honesty rule</h2>
      <p>
         Applicability is not a pass or fail. It is triage. If the runtime says a criterion is
         applicable but coverage is manual-only, that is not a defect in the engine. It is a warning to
         stop pretending automation can do more than it can.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
